Appendix G: Full-Chain PFHd Allocation

G.1 PFHd Calculation Methodology

Definition G.1 (PFHd). The Probability of Dangerous Failure per Hour for a safety function is:

\text{PFHd} = \frac{1 - \text{DC}}{MTTFd}

For a subsystem with multiple components, the total PFHd is the sum:

\text{PFHd}_{\text{total}} = \sum_{i=1}^{n} \text{PFHd}_i

SISTEMA is the standard software tool to calculate PL and PFHd for the implementation of EN ISO 13849-1. The PFHd calculations are based on the conservative assumption that all potential faults of any component in the safety-related parts of the control system are dangerous.

