K.2 Confidence Bounds

Theorem K.1 (Statistical Confidence Bound). For zero failures in n independent trials, the upper bound on failure probability at confidence level 1 - \alpha is:

p_{\text{upper}} = 1 - \alpha^{1/n}

Proof. The probability of zero failures in n trials with failure probability p is (1-p)^n. Setting (1-p)^n = \alpha and solving for p:

p_{\text{upper}} = 1 - \alpha^{1/n}

For n = 300 and \alpha = 0.05, p_{\text{upper}} \approx 1\%. \square

