Appendix M: Notified Body Engagement Strategy

M.1 Certification Bottleneck

Certification timelines are excessively long due to the shortage of Notified Bodies (NB). Costs vary significantly, and interpretations of requirements differ, creating inefficiency and uncertainty. The EU Machinery Regulation 2023/1230 introduces third-party Notified Body assessment for safety-related software control systems that include AI or have adaptive behavior.

M.2 Pre-Submission Strategy

1. Safety Case Development: Build a Goal Structuring Notation (GSN) safety case from project inception (Appendix I).
2. Formal Proof Evidence: Provide the KeYmaera X proof certificate of Theorem 3.2 as evidence for the safety claim.
3. Hardware Validation Data: Include measured brake deceleration, reaction time, and wheel slip curves as evidence for model parameters.
4. Assumption Documentation: Document all assumptions and their validity conditions.
5. Runtime Evidence Log: Include a tamper-evident log that records every safety monitor decision.

M.3 Engagement Timeline

Phase Timeline Key Deliverables
1. Formal Foundation 0–6 months Complete KeYmaera X proof; publish formal specification
